Unix utility 'hash'

The Unix utility 'hash' is closer to a Unix like shell. He doesn't care about extension of files,
but for those that have some extension, it must be provided. 'hash' will be the new Hexagonix
shell, receiving new functions from according to the evolution of the system.

A command can be started in the background instead of blocking the shell until it finishes. To do
this, add an ampersand character at the end of the command line, for example 'clock &'. The shell
shows the process identification number of the new process right away, which can later be used
with the 'kill' utility to terminate it.

USAGE:

hash

No additional parameters are required.

For more information, enter 'hash ?' or 'hash --help'.

HISTORY

This command appeared in the Hexagonix H1 or in previous development versions (2015-2021).

